    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d828">

                <pb facs="0678" n="670" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg670"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51 Con-Ob American Group/42</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Minister of Finance</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kung</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the American, Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)<anchor n="96"
                        xml:id="d828-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-03-31">March 31, 1937</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Ambassador Johnson</hi>: Now that the Hukuang
                    and Chicago Bank loan settlements have been effected I desire to take up the
                    case of the Pacific Development Loan. To this end I should appreciate your
                    transmitting by telegraph, as you recently were good enough to do in the case of
                    the Hukuang and Chicago loans, the attached communication to Mr. Lamont<anchor
                        n="97" xml:id="d828-f2"/> of Messrs. J. P. Morgan &amp; Company which
                    contains a proposal of settlement. Also I should appreciate having a copy
                    furnished to the Chinese Ambassador at Washington.</p>
                <p>Yours faithfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. H. Kung</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d828-f1" n="96" type="source" xml:id="d828-f1-content">
                <p>Copy transmitted to the Department by the Ambassador in his despatch No. 415,
                    April 9; received May 3.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d828-f2" n="97" xml:id="d828-f2-content">
                <p>Thomas W. Lamont, representing the American group of the China Consortium.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
